Hi Erin,

Skimming the metadata of your rasters (link <https://s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/www.cacpd.org/climate_normals/NA_ReadMe.txt>), I noticed that your original rasters are using a Lambert Conformal Conic projection. So,  you need to reproject to a longitude/latitude projection instead of define projection. You can use the raster::projectRaster() function to do that (please, check the documentation of the function). This is the projection that you need to use on Wallace: "+proj=longlat +ellps=WGS84 +datum=WGS84 +no_defs".

Here is some material that I think that can help you
https://geocompr.robinlovelace.net/reproj-geo-data.html#reprojecting-raster-geometries
https://weiming-hu.github.io/projection-in-R/#projection-1-north-america-lambert-conformal-conic

Let me know if the information is useful.

Best,
Gonzalo

